# =============================================================================
# Docker build context exclusions.
#
# The build context is the whole repository root (the Dockerfile needs uv.lock
# and the sibling workspace packages), so this file is what keeps key material,
# local state and tooling caches out of the daemon's hands. Anything listed
# here cannot end up in an image layer even by accident -- including in an
# intermediate layer that `docker history` would still expose.
#
# The first section mirrors the secret patterns in .gitignore. It is duplicated
# rather than referenced because the two mechanisms are independent: a file
# that is git-ignored is still perfectly visible to `docker build`, and a
# working tree that has been used for local testing WILL contain the CA output
# directory this excludes.
# =============================================================================

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Key material and secrets -- deny by default
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.crt
**/*.cer
**/*.der
**/*.csr
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
**/*.jks
**/*.keystore
**/*.gpg
**/*.asc
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/secrets/
**/*.pat

# The whole CA directory. Its private/ subdirectory holds the issuing key and
# out/ holds every member's material. None of it belongs anywhere near an
# image, and the running containers receive what they need through mounts.
deploy/ca/

# WireGuard configurations contain private keys and pre-shared keys.
deploy/wireguard/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deployment material that is mounted, never built in
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# nginx configuration reaches the proxy as a read-only bind mount, so a copy
# inside the application image would only ever be a stale decoy during an
# incident review.
deploy/
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.dev.yml

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local state that would bloat or poison the image
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .git carries the full history: every secret ever committed and reverted, and
# tens of megabytes of objects. It is the single most common way a credential
# reaches a published image.
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github/
.claude/

# A host virtualenv contains absolute paths and host-architecture binaries. If
# it were copied in it could shadow the image's own environment.
.venv/
venv/
env/

**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.so
**/*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.eggs/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tooling caches and reports
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.hypothesis/
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
junit*.xml
bandit-report.json
pip-audit-report.json
semgrep-report.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tests and developer material
#
# Excluded from the image both to keep it small and to remove code paths: test
# fixtures generate certificates and construct permissive Settings objects, and
# none of that should be present in a production container.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
**/tests/
**/conftest.py
docs/
demo/
scripts/
LICENSE

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editors, OS and logs
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
**/*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
**/*.log
pgdata/
.local/
.aivs-dev/
